{"tc":{"ruleId":"0va7u6","ruleName":"HTML images contain no text","testcaseId":"6a7f199a37309ccab08941b0bc64e182770c29ac","expected":"failed","sc":["1.4.5"],"localPath":"pages/0va7u6/6a7f199a37309ccab08941b0bc64e182770c29ac.html","url":"https://www.w3.org/WAI/content-assets/wcag-act-rules/testcases/0va7u6/6a7f199a37309ccab08941b0bc64e182770c29ac.html","draft":false},"agentSubjects":[],"rubricSubjects":[{"xpath":"/html/body/img[1]","sc":"1.4.5","claimFamily":"images-of-text","rubricId":"images-of-text-v0","rubric":{"id":"images-of-text-v0","sc":"1.4.5","skill":"color-and-visual-text","visionEvidence":["element-crop","surrounding-region"],"text":"# 1.4.5 — images of text (v0 atomic rubric)\n\n**Division of labor (v3.2).** You do NOT investigate the page and you do NOT run OCR. The collector\nidentified an image element (an `<img>`, `role=img`, SVG/canvas drawing) and screenshotted its rendered\npixels. No deterministic tool can tell a raster of TEXT from a photo, so the obligation is auto-PARTIAL\nand handed to you. JUDGE the pixels. Where a deterministic CLAIM already disposed this obligation, DEFER.\n\n**Judge:** does the image RENDER TEXT — words, sentences, labels, or a heading drawn as a picture — that\nconveys information and **could be presented as real, selectable HTML text** instead? If the meaningful\ncontent of the image IS text baked into the bitmap (a JPEG of a paragraph, a heading saved as a PNG, a\n\"button\" whose label is part of the image), that IS a 1.4.5 barrier (REPRODUCED) — author it as text.\n\n**This is NOT a barrier (do not flag):**\n- **Logotypes / wordmarks / brand names** — text that is part of a logo is the ESSENTIAL exception\n  (the W3C / a company logo with its name in it is fine).\n- **Essential presentation** — text whose particular visual form is the point: a screenshot/diagram\n  demonstrating an interface, a chart/graph with axis labels, sample renderings, signatures, a font\n  specimen, mathematical/code imagery where layout carries meaning.\n- **Images with no meaningful text** — photos, icons, illustrations, decorative graphics. Incidental\n  text inside a photograph (a street sign in a snapshot) is not the image's conveyed content.\n\n**Evidence handed to you:** the `element-crop` (the image's rendered pixels) and `surrounding-region`\n(to see whether the same text also appears as real text nearby, which can change the call), plus the\nelement's role/accessible name as context.\n\n**WCAG soundness caveats (do NOT manufacture a failure these don't support):**\n- This rubric owns ONLY *images of text* (1.4.5). Do NOT judge whether the alt text is adequate (1.1.1),\n  the contrast of the rendered text (1.4.3), or sizing — other rubrics own those.\n- Seeing the pixels is REQUIRED: if the `element-crop` is blank, transparent, or unrendered (an SVG/canvas\n  captured before it painted, a remote/relative asset that 404s — e.g. under `file://`, leaving a\n  broken-image glyph), you cannot tell text-image from photo — return PARTIAL, do not guess. (A normally\n  rendered SVG/canvas that DID paint is fine to judge — the trigger is BLANK PIXELS, not the element type.)\n- A small amount of incidental/decorative lettering is not the same as an image whose PURPOSE is to\n  present a block of textual content — judge what the image is FOR.\n- When it is genuinely ambiguous whether the rendered text is a logo/essential case vs. avoidable\n  text-as-image, return PARTIAL rather than over-flagging.\n- If the `svgLiveText` signal is present (an `<svg>` rendering live `<text>`/`<tspan>`), the text is REAL and\n  machine-readable, NOT flattened pixels — it is NOT an image of text and carries no 1.4.5 barrier (NOT\n  REPRODUCED). 1.4.5 targets text BAKED INTO a raster/painted image, not accessible vector text.\n\n**Output:** STRICT JSON `{verdict, confidence, summary, reasoning, evidenceRefs}`. verdict ∈\n{REPRODUCED (barrier — meaningful text presented as an image that could be real text), NOT REPRODUCED\n(no barrier — logo/essential/no-meaningful-text), PARTIAL (cannot decide from the crop), N/A (abstain —\nNOT \"out of scope\", that is the oracle's job)}.","promptHash":"sha256:7a786d7506763a9f29d6bc053e7edb14c497a0c23d410d591d63562658b8d9a8"},"skill":"color-and-visual-text","element":{"xpath":"/html/body/img[1]","text":"","hasText":false,"inactiveText":false,"sectionHeading":null,"focusable":false,"isInteractive":false,"isFormField":false,"isImage":true,"ariaAttrs":[],"roleAttr":"","sampledRole":"img","axRole":"img","axName":"WCAG Rocks","tag":"img","type":"","href":null,"jsHref":null,"htmlSnippet":"<img alt=\"WCAG Rocks\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,\n\t&lt;svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' height='20px' width='80px'&gt;\n\t  &lt;text x='0' y='15'&gt;WCAG Rocks&lt;/text&gt;\n\t&lt;/svg&gt;\">","enclosingHtml":"<body>\n\t<img alt=\"WCAG Rocks\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,\n\t&lt;svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' height='20px' width='80px'&gt;\n\t  &lt;text x='0' y='15'&gt;WCAG Rocks&lt;/text&gt;\n\t&lt;/svg&gt;\">\n\n</body>","ariaLevel":null,"box":{"x":8,"y":8,"width":80,"height":20},"inModal":false,"focusRisk":false,"removedFromA11yTree":false,"hiddenMechanism":null,"renderedVisible":true,"svgLiveText":false,"svgNamedDescendant":false,"ariaHiddenWithName":false,"complexImageHint":false,"tabindexEffective":null,"hasGlyphText":false,"splitFieldGroup":false,"roleOverridesNative":false,"placeholder":null,"liveRegion":false,"isMedia":false,"mediaInfo":null,"autoMotion":false,"underOverlay":false,"hasHoverContent":false,"backgroundImageMeaningful":false,"backgroundImageUrl":null,"isCaptcha":false,"iframeTabExcluded":false,"focusableInAriaHidden":false,"prohibitedAriaAttr":false,"cdpRole":"image","inTree":true,"ignoredByModal":false,"applicableScs":["1.1.1","1.4.11","1.4.5"]}}],"pOpts":{"toolsEnabled":false,"transcriptByXpath":null,"visionByXpath":{"/html/body/img[1]":{"element-crop":"","surrounding-region":"","viewport":"","viewport-320":""}},"checkerHintsByXpath":{},"file":"act:6a7f199a37309ccab08941b0bc64e182770c29ac","runId":"fp-6a7f199a37309ccab08941b0bc64e182770c29ac","pageDigest":"sha256:url:708d6feed3f6b606eaba097ccba912ecc323425285369ed23668549bfc48ba7d","llmConcurrency":40},"built":{"ok":true,"results":{"shadowObservations":[],"obligationLedger":[{"obligationId":"/html/body/img[1]::1.4.11::non-text-contrast","xpath":"/html/body/img[1]","sc":"1.4.11","claimFamily":"non-text-contrast","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/html/body/img[1]::1.1.1::non-text-content","xpath":"/html/body/img[1]","sc":"1.1.1","claimFamily":"non-text-content","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/html/body/img[1]::1.4.5::images-of-text","xpath":"/html/body/img[1]","sc":"1.4.5","claimFamily":"images-of-text","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/page-level::title::2.4.2::page-title","xpath":"/page-level::title","sc":"2.4.2","claimFamily":"page-title","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/page-level::info-relationships::1.3.1::info-relationships","xpath":"/page-level::info-relationships","sc":"1.3.1","claimFamily":"info-relationships","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/page-level::section-headings::2.4.10::section-headings","xpath":"/page-level::section-headings","sc":"2.4.10","claimFamily":"section-headings","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false},{"obligationId":"/page-level::focus-order::2.4.3::focus-order-meaning","xpath":"/page-level::focus-order","sc":"2.4.3","claimFamily":"focus-order-meaning","disposition":"PARTIAL","cleared":false,"autoPartial":true,"shadow":false}]}}}